# Diagrams

## Mermaid or draw.io

Mermaid is allowed only for very small diagrams, where automatic layout
cannot get messy:

- a flowchart with about five nodes or fewer, one direction, no subgraphs
- a sequence diagram with at most three participants and a few messages

Anything larger, or anything where arrows would cross or need routing, is a
draw.io diagram.

## Format

- Save each diagram as one editable `.drawio.svg`: an SVG export with the
  diagram embedded, so it renders in the docs and opens directly in draw.io.
  Do not add a separate `.drawio`, `.png`, or plain `.svg` copy.
- Export with the adaptive theme and a solid background, so it follows the
  site's light/dark toggle:
  `draw.io -x -f svg -e --embed-svg-fonts false --theme auto -b 16 -o out.drawio.svg in.drawio`
- The Docusaurus build prints one "can't be read correctly" warning per
  `.drawio.svg` reference. That is expected (draw.io's embedded diagram
  defeats the image-size check); do not work around it.

## Location

Put diagrams in a folder named after the Markdown file, next to it. Name each
file after what it shows, without repeating the page name.

```
docs/docs/gitdb/connectivity.md
docs/docs/gitdb/connectivity/topology.drawio.svg
docs/docs/gitdb/connectivity/first-device-join.drawio.svg
```

Reference it with a relative path:

```markdown
![Topology: devices, hosted services, and the home host](./connectivity/topology.drawio.svg)
```

A diagram used by several pages lives with the page that defines the concept;
other pages reference that file instead of copying it.
